WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.110
But then he also had this candidness
about him, this soft-spokenness about

2
00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:09.820
him. When you wanted to talk about
something serious, he was there.

3
00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:13.750
And I do remember a couple times,
you know, when he was at our house,

4
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:16.970
at the pool house, he and I would
have these really deep conversations.

5
00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:20.170
I was in my 20s, and I was trying to
figure out what the heck I was going

6
00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:23.310
to do. And he and I would just
talk, and he would listen.

7
00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:25.260
And it was a beautiful relationship.

8
00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:27.920
So I miss him dearly. I love you all.

9
00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:33.730
And here's to Uncle Moshe, who would
always call me every year on my birthday,

10
00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:36.980
or actually any time, and sing to me:

11
00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:45.310
I love you so much, Daniel. And
I hope you all get to feel that

12
00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:49.430
love, because to each and every
one of you, I love you so much.
